title: Authorizations › Eligibility & Benefits › List › The info icon
route: /authorizations/eligibility
intro: The text of the old 'Why we check twice' banner sits behind a small info icon beside the page title. It opens on hover, on keyboard focus and on a click, and closes on Escape, on a click elsewhere, or when the pointer and focus leave. The icon is a button with aria-expanded.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "On the list, look at the title\n'28 of 37 patients are cleared to bill.'"
screen ic "Small info icon after the title\nName for screen readers: 'Why we check twice'"
click h1 "Move the pointer onto the icon"
click f1 "Tab to the icon (keyboard focus)"
click c1 "Click the icon"
overlay tp "Info tip under the title\n'Why we check twice. Eligibility says the patient is covered.\nBenefits say the service is payable. For Medicaid programs the second one\ndecides whether the clinic is reimbursed, even when the copay is $0.'"
process ae "aria-expanded is true while the tip is open\nThe text is the icon's description"
decision q1 "How was it opened?"
click l1 "Move the pointer away"
click b1 "Tab away from the icon"
click k1 "Click the icon again, or press Escape"
click o1 "Click anywhere else on the page"
process cl "Tip closes\nA pop-up above it stays: Escape closes one layer at a time"
process keep "A click opens it and keeps it open\nuntil Escape, a second click or a click elsewhere"
end e1 "Page as before, no banner"

s1 --> ic
ic --> h1 --> tp
ic --> f1 --> tp
ic --> c1 --> tp
tp --> ae --> q1
q1 -->|Pointer| l1 --> cl
q1 -->|Focus| b1 --> cl
q1 -->|Click| keep
keep --> k1 --> cl
keep --> o1 --> cl
cl --> e1
